\DIFaddend \subsection{Datasets and representative workflows}

Two public datasets and one private dataset were used for workflow validation. The Tufts Dental Database (TDD) \cite{panetta2022tufts} was used for 2D panoramic radiograph segmentation. Its panoramic images and tooth-level annotations were reformatted into a 32-class tooth segmentation task, with each class corresponding to an individual tooth label. After automated auditing and eligibility checking, 968 of 1051 cases were retained. This dataset was used for both panoramic workflow validation and the skill-based configuration case study.

ToothFairy \cite{ToothFairyDataset1, ToothFairyDataset2, ToothFairyDataset3} was used for 3D CBCT segmentation. Together, the TDD and ToothFairy datasets represent two common dental imaging scenarios with different dimensionality, data organization, preprocessing requirements, metadata structures, and model execution logic.

In addition, a private labeled panoramic radiograph dataset was used for downstream lesion detection validation. It included 290 panoramic radiographs collected during routine clinical care at our hospital between 2012 and 2024 under ethical approval PKUSSIRB-2025,107,012. Each image was annotated with bounding boxes for pulp, root canal fillings, fillings, and periapical lesions by clinical experts, and images with poor quality, severe artifacts, incomplete dentition coverage, or uncommon anatomical conditions that could compromise annotation reliability were excluded. The radiographs were acquired using a Planmeca dental panoramic X-ray system and stored as 8-bit grayscale JPEG images. The cohort had a mean age of 35.6 years, with a standard deviation of 15.2 years and a range of 16 to 80 years, and the gender distribution was 51\% male and 49\% female.

\DIFaddbegin \DIFadd{In addition to single-model inference, the platform supported test-time
augmentation (TTA) and multi-model ensemble inference through a dedicated module
(}\texttt{\DIFadd{tta\_ensemble.py}}\DIFadd{). Six geometric transforms (identity, horizontal flip,
vertical flip, 90$^\circ$/180$^\circ$/270$^\circ$ rotation) were applied to each
