\subsection{Structured reporting and review-oriented outputs}

Beyond workflow execution itself, DentalClaw generated structured outputs intended to support result review, workflow traceability, and experiment comparison. For each validated task, the platform exported workflow metadata, preparation summaries, model configuration records, quantitative evaluation tables, prediction files, and case-level notes in a unified output format. These outputs were designed to move beyond raw model predictions and provide a review-oriented representation of the completed workflow.

A representative report generated by DentalClaw is shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:report_figure}. The report was organized around three layers of information: (1) workflow-level metadata describing the executed task and dataset context, (2) quantitative results summarizing model performance and generated outputs, and (3) case-level notes highlighting review-relevant findings and failure-prone cases. In this way, the final report preserved not only what the model produced, but also how the experiment was configured and which intermediate outputs were generated during execution.

This reporting capability was observed in both the 2D panoramic and 3D CBCT workflows, indicating that DentalClaw can standardize not only task execution but also result presentation across modalities. Such outputs may facilitate experiment tracking, workflow comparison, and expert review in future dental imaging studies.

